<KkShell
  title="SEO Agency (Preview)"
  description="SEO for businesses that want to be found by the people typing it in, in the Dead River look."
  kicker="SEO"
  headline="SHOW UP WHEN THEY SEARCH. WITHOUT DOING ANYTHING GOOGLE WILL PUNISH YOU FOR."
  sub="Rankings don't pay the crew. Calls do. We do SEO for the calls."
  faqTitle="SEO, STRAIGHT ANSWERS"
  faqs={faqs}
>
  <p class="kk-dear">Hey,</p>
  <p>Here's the honest version of SEO, from somebody who has watched a lot of businesses pay for it and get nothing.</p>
  <p>When somebody in your city types what you sell into Google, there are two places that get most of the clicks. The map with the three businesses on it, and the free results underneath. If you're not in either one, you don't exist to that person. They call whoever is.</p>
  <p>And those clicks don't cost you anything. That's why they're the most valuable traffic there is.</p>
  <p>So why do most businesses give up on it?</p>
  <h2>BECAUSE THEY GOT BURNED</h2>
  <p>Maybe you've paid for SEO before. Somebody sold you "page one rankings," and maybe they even got you there. For "left-handed plumber in northeast El Paso." A search nobody types.</p>
  <p>Or they sent a report every month with a lot of charts going up, and the phone stayed the same.</p>
  <p>Here's what they don't tell you. Rankings aren't the goal. You can't take rankings to the bank, you can't pay your crew with them, and you sure can't make a truck payment with them. The only thing that matters is whether more people called and more of them became customers.</p>
  <h2>AND THE SHORTCUTS GOT THEM PENALIZED</h2>
  <p>A lot of SEO agencies rank sites with tricks. Networks of junk blogs that exist only to link to clients. Bought links. Fake business listings in towns you don't serve. Pages stuffed with the city name swapped out fifty times.</p>
  <p>It works, until Google figures it out. Then your site drops off the face of the earth and the agency that did it is long gone. We've had clients come to us after that happened. Some of it you can fix. Some of it means starting over with a new domain.</p>
  <p>We don't do any of it. Everything we do, you could show Google and be fine.</p>
  <h2>WHAT ACTUALLY MOVES THE PHONE</h2>
  <ul class="kk-list">
    <li><strong>One page for each thing you sell.</strong> Google ranks pages, not businesses. One page for "plumbing" loses to one page for each thing you fix, with what's included, what changes the price, real photos, and a phone number.</li>
    <li><strong>A Google profile that's right.</strong> Real name, real category, real service area, real hours, real photos of real work. The map pack is the front door for a business people come to or who come to you, and most profiles are half empty.</li>
    <li><strong>Reviews, asked for every time.</strong> Every customer gets the same ask, by text, one tap. The businesses with the reviews get the map spot. It's that simple and almost nobody does it.</li>
    <li><strong>Answers to the questions people actually ask.</strong> "How much is a new water heater." "How many sessions until I see a difference." A short honest answer on your site, with what changes it. That's what Google ranks now, and it's what the AI search tools pull from too.</li>
    <li><strong>A site that works on a phone.</strong> Loads fast, the form works, the number is tappable. Most of your customers are reading on a phone in a parking lot.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>No magic. Just the stuff that works, done every month, measured by calls instead of charts.</p>
  <h2>WHY WE DON'T SELL SEO ON ITS OWN</h2>
  <p>SEO takes months. You need the phone to ring this month. So we run it alongside Google Ads and the Demand Intelligence list, which get you in front of the people searching right now, while the free results build underneath. By the time the SEO is carrying weight, the ads have paid for it.</p>
  <p>And the whole thing is under one guarantee. $50,000 in new revenue in 45-60 days, or your money back, plus $500 for wasting your time. Not rankings. Revenue.</p>
  <p class="kk-ps">P.S. The search pages in Marketing is F*cking Easy walk through every one of the five things above, with the checklists. It's free, further down this page.</p>
</KkShell>
